brcm-dma.resource/BDMA_QueryInfoTagList             brcm-dma.resource/BDMA_QueryInfoTagList

   NAME
	BDMA_QueryInfoTagList -- what the engine is (V0.1)

   SYNOPSIS
	answers = BDMA_QueryInfoTagList( tagList )
	d0                           a0

	ULONG BDMA_QueryInfoTagList(CONST struct TagItem *);

   FUNCTION
	As GetDTAttrs() does: each tag names an attribute and the ULONG * that goes with it receives the value. A tag that this version does not know is
	skipped and its place left alone (a client that asks for something newer puts a sentinel in it first). The engine starts with the first call that
	needs to know.

   INPUTS
	tagList         BDI_Available    TRUE when an engine runs and proved itself
	                BDI_Version      (version << 16) | revision of the resource
	                BDI_Interrupt    TRUE when the end of a job comes by interrupt
	                BDI_Model        BDM_BCM2711 (Pi 4B, 400, CM4) or BDM_BCM2835 (the family of the Zero, Pi 2, Pi 3: not written)
	                BDI_Features     BDFF_RECT, BDFF_BIGBLOCKS, BDFF_MOVE, BDFF_WIDE, BDFF_FILL
	                BDI_Channels     the mask of the channels that the resource manages
	                BDI_Classes      BDCLASS_*, the classes of those channels
	                BDI_VideoBase    the memory of the RTG board, which the CPU does not cache (0 if none)
	                BDI_VideoSize    its size
	                BDI_MaxRows      the limit: the most rows a rectangle job may have
	                BDI_Jobs         jobs done since the start
	                BDI_MegaBytes    megabytes moved since the start
	                BDI_Failures     jobs that failed
	                BDI_QueueMax     the most jobs ever waiting in the queue at once
	                BDI_WaitMaxUs    the longest stay in the queue before a slice went on a channel, microseconds
	                BDI_Aborts       jobs aborted
	                BDI_Timeouts     slices given up by the watchdog
	                BDI_Busy         BDJ_NoWait jobs refused (BDERR_BUSY)
	                BDI_Slices       times a big job went back to the queue for its next slice
	                BDI_Deferred     jobs held back by a conflict while a channel was idle
	                BDI_BusyMs0      milliseconds the first channel ran slices
	                BDI_BusyMs1      the same, second channel
	                BDI_Size64       jobs done of up to 64 bytes (length x rows)
	                BDI_Size4K       of up to 4 KB
	                BDI_Size32K      of up to 32 KB
	                BDI_Size1M       of up to 1 MB
	                BDI_SizeBig      of more than 1 MB
	                BDI_IrqCalls     interrupts of the channels that ended a slice
	                BDI_IrqMCycles   what they cost the CPU in megacycles (2^20 cycles), from the counters of Emu68 read in the interrupt
	                BDI_IrqKInstr    and in 68k instructions, in thousands (2^10)

   RESULTS
	answers         the number of values written

   EXAMPLES
	BDMA_QueryInfoTags(BDI_Available, &available, BDI_Classes, &classes, TAG_DONE);

   NOTES
	A task context.

